WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:05.380
When you think of the biggest, most money-making,
merchandised and capitalized game series of

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:10.580
all time, there’s only one franchise that
comes to mind: Pokémon.

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:16.331
For the entirety of its lifespan, Pokémon
has been a financial powerhouse, and every

00:00:16.331 --> 00:00:20.359
year the series seems to grow in popularity
and revenue.

00:00:20.359 --> 00:00:26.349
Whether it’s games, cards, a show, toys,
or even Pokémon-branded clothes that you

00:00:26.349 --> 00:00:30.990
need, you’ll have no difficulty finding
a product that appeals to you.

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:35.829
Everyone knows Pikachu’s face, and nearly
every child born within the past twenty years

00:00:35.829 --> 00:00:38.809
has had firsthand experience with Pokémon.

00:00:38.809 --> 00:00:41.710
It is, in some respects, inescapable.

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:46.859
If you hate Pokémon, too bad, because this
little electric mouse runs this world, and

00:00:46.859 --> 00:00:49.359
you’ll just have to sit back and deal with
it.

00:00:49.359 --> 00:00:53.110
One could even say that Pokémon is uncontainable.

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:59.250
Which poses quite the issue for the SCP Foundation,
who work tirelessly to ensure that no facet

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:01.530
of life is withheld from its reach.

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:06.750
But the Foundation rarely deals with major
franchises, beloved by millions upon millions

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:10.780
of people across the world, and for good reason
too.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:15.900
An anomaly tied in with a major franchise
poses a lot of problems on the containment

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:16.900
side.

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:22.080
Namely, its ability to spread uncontrollably
and without care, being witnessed by countless

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:26.190
individuals before the Foundation comes up
with a way to contain it.

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:30.250
Global supply lines have to be interrupted
to prevent anomalous products from hitting

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:35.820
shelves, corporate espionage committed, and
most of all, a massively expensive cover-up

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:39.380
operation to remove said products from consumer’s
hands.

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:44.490
If the Foundation had to deal with an anomaly
affecting the Pokémon franchise, there’s

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:50.630
no telling how out of hand it would get before
they’d be able to get a handle on the situation.

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:54.300
But in 2019, that’s exactly what happened.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:02:00.980
Today we’re going to be looking at SCP-5254,
an anomaly dubbed “Gotta Catch ‘Em All”

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:02.890
in the Foundation’s database.

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:09.110
The year was 2019, the place Japan, the home
country of the Pokémon franchise.

00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:14.780
Every year since 2014, the Pokémon Company
has held a festival named “Pikachu Outbreak!”

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:19.200
in the city of Yokohama, in which hundreds
of costumed actors dressed as Pikachu would

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:25.140
crowd the city’s Mirai district, and perform,
dance, and even participate in a parade.

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:29.640
The event was intended to celebrate the Pokémon
franchise and promote whatever the latest

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:34.730
venture the series is pushing, whether it's
a game, a movie, or something else.

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:39.160
The festival proved to be successful and has
been held every year since.

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:43.860
After all, who wouldn’t want to see a legion
of Pikachu running amok through the streets?

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:49.120
But the fun would be short-lived during the
2019 Outbreak, where something incredibly

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:51.160
unusual occurred.

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:56.500
Picture this, a large crowd, hundreds of fans
dressed in Pokémon-themed attire, standing

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:58.370
on both sides of the streets.

00:02:58.370 --> 00:03:04.440
Men, women, children, anyone and everyone
came to see the Pikachu Outbreak, and they

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:05.880
weren’t disappointed.

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:10.250
Parading down the street was a hoard of Pikachu,
just as advertised.

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:16.150
They danced, bounced, and walked together
in routine fashion, all while the crowd cheered

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:17.160
and yelled.

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:21.690
Even the spectators in the crowd showed their
spirit with Pikachu-themed hats, yellow tails

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:27.550
fastened to their backs, and yellow face masks
with two electrified red circles on the cheeks.

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:32.849
The parade proceeded as normal, that is, until
one of the parading Pikachu started behaving

00:03:32.849 --> 00:03:33.849
oddly.

00:03:33.849 --> 00:03:39.099
It began as out-of-sync movements, strange
wobbles and deviations from the parade path.

00:03:39.099 --> 00:03:43.340
For the heavily coordinated Outbreak festival,
this was unusual.

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:47.240
The rest of the Pikachu line danced to the
beat of the music, sticking in formation as

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:48.450
best as they could.

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:53.880
Then, as if pushed by an invisible force,
the strange Pikachu raced forward, diving

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:59.450
head first into the crowd, barreling into
the group of people and eventually colliding.

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:05.560
The crowd moved out of the way, slightly shocked
- no pun intended - by what had occurred.

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:07.120
But then it happened again!

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:09.290
Two more Pikachu ran into the crowd.

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:10.319
And then again!

00:04:10.319 --> 00:04:15.970
Over fifteen Pikachu ran themselves into the
crowd, resulting in a massive disruption of

00:04:15.970 --> 00:04:19.549
the parade, and the shut-down of the event
entirely.

00:04:19.549 --> 00:04:23.430
The Foundation quickly caught wind of this,
and sent their closest operatives to assess

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:26.219
the situation in a controlled fashion.

00:04:26.219 --> 00:04:31.400
After blocking off the crowd and shutting
down the event, another strange detail emerged,

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:35.870
one that ensured the Foundation that there
had to be some sort of anomalous significance

00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:37.889
to what was occurring here.

00:04:37.889 --> 00:04:42.249
Some of the crowd members involved in the
collisions were suffering very peculiar medical

00:04:42.249 --> 00:04:48.050
injuries, namely blunt force trauma way stronger
than what a clash with a costumed actor would

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:51.499
induce, and severe electrical burns.

00:04:51.499 --> 00:04:56.210
The Foundation was positive there was something
occurring here, and with a franchise as vast

00:04:56.210 --> 00:05:00.250
and popular as Pokémon, they didn’t want
to take any chances.

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:04.969
Immediately, Foundation agents began collecting
information on the event, setting up probes

00:05:04.969 --> 00:05:09.680
in the offices of Gamefreak and The Pokémon
Company, and attempting to get to the bottom

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:12.169
of what exactly happened during the parade.

00:05:12.169 --> 00:05:16.999
When the Foundation interrogated the 15 mascots
who collided with the crowd, they were shocked

00:05:16.999 --> 00:05:22.099
to learn that they weren’t mascots at all,
but instead fully separate entities that resembled

00:05:22.099 --> 00:05:23.960
the Pikachu costume.

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:29.330
X-Rays revealed that their once human skeletons
were now fused to their costumes, and touching

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:32.020
them produced a minor electric shock.

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:36.939
The performers had become Pikachu, and now
they were unable to be removed from their

00:05:36.939 --> 00:05:38.279
costumes.

00:05:38.279 --> 00:05:42.770
Every captured instance had expired before
the Foundation was able to fully study and

00:05:42.770 --> 00:05:47.550
discern what was occuring to them, their bodies
unable to support themselves after such a

00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:50.199
lethal, extreme transformation.

00:05:50.199 --> 00:05:54.860
Later observation found that the synthetic
components of the costumes, such as the cotton

00:05:54.860 --> 00:05:59.789
and plastic composites, had fused into their
flesh and muscle tissue.

00:05:59.789 --> 00:06:04.930
Bodily fluids were found to contain foriegn
DNA and numerous strange structures, to the

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:10.029
point where an ordinary human’s genetic
makeup would be incomparable and unrecognizable

00:06:10.029 --> 00:06:12.349
with that affected by the anomaly.

00:06:12.349 --> 00:06:18.150
The Foundation tentatively opened a file on
SCP-5254, the anomalous transformation of

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:23.219
a human into the rough approximation of a
Pokémon character, and began carrying out

00:06:23.219 --> 00:06:26.409
tests to determine what occurred during the
festival.

00:06:26.409 --> 00:06:28.960
What caused SCP-5254 to manifest?

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:31.939
It couldn’t have been random, could it?

00:06:31.939 --> 00:06:34.629
The Foundation needed to know.

00:06:34.629 --> 00:06:39.560
One theory that researchers working on the
SCP-5254 file had come up with was that it

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:44.490
was the large gathering of Pokémon related
clothing worn by the crowd that prompted the

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:45.539
transformation.

00:06:45.539 --> 00:06:49.919
But that begged the question, why hadn’t
this occurred at any previous festivals or

00:06:49.919 --> 00:06:52.300
large Pokémon related gatherings?

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:57.279
It was a huge franchise, there were absolutely
more events that had masses of costumed fans

00:06:57.279 --> 00:06:59.219
donning Pokémon-related gear.

00:06:59.219 --> 00:07:02.590
Did something happen in recent years to manifest
this anomaly?

00:07:02.590 --> 00:07:05.509
The only way to find out was to conduct testing.

00:07:05.509 --> 00:07:10.309
In one of the easier experiments that a D-Class
personnel was tasked with carrying out, the

00:07:10.309 --> 00:07:15.100
Foundation ordered a group of them to dress
entirely in Pokémon-related clothing, which

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:17.550
the Foundation provided themselves.

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:21.889
Some items, such as a full-bodied Gardevoir
onesie, were taken from Dr. Clef’s personal

00:07:21.889 --> 00:07:23.069
collection itself!

00:07:23.069 --> 00:07:26.039
No, he is not taking further questions.

00:07:26.039 --> 00:07:30.839
Anyways, with the D-Class looking utterly
ridiculous in full Pokémon getup, the observing

00:07:30.839 --> 00:07:33.259
researchers began their tests.

00:07:33.259 --> 00:07:38.360
First was a D-Class outfitted solely in a
“Pokémon Pikachu Big Face with Ears Hat.”,

00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:40.699
as the product’s official title stated.

00:07:40.699 --> 00:07:46.220
After standing there for 15 minutes, the Foundation
determined that there was no discernible effect.

00:07:46.220 --> 00:07:50.319
Next was a “Pokemon Detective Pikachu Cosplay
Mask Latex”

00:07:50.319 --> 00:07:53.149
, which the Foundation placed on the same
D-Class.

00:07:53.149 --> 00:07:58.280
After another 15 minutes with no changes observed,
the D-Class closed the experiment, remarking

00:07:58.280 --> 00:08:00.020
that it was stupid.

00:08:00.020 --> 00:08:04.150
The Research team told the D-Class to remain
composed and to just continue along with the

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:07.199
trials unless they wanted to be reprimanded.

00:08:07.199 --> 00:08:11.369
After that was a “D'BOON Adult Onesie Pikachu
Animal Pajamas”.

00:08:11.369 --> 00:08:16.059
A few researchers held back laughter as the
hardened, muscular D-Class in front of them

00:08:16.059 --> 00:08:19.669
stood around in a Pikachu onesie that barely
fit him.

00:08:19.669 --> 00:08:23.930
After asking him how he was feeling, the subject
quickly turned aggressive.

00:08:23.930 --> 00:08:29.069
The results from this test were deemed inconclusive,
due to researchers being unable to determine

00:08:29.069 --> 00:08:34.500
if the quick snap in anger was a result of
a potential anomaly or whether the D-Class

00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:37.000
was just getting fed up with having to do
this.

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:44.889
For the next test, two D-Class were brought
in, clad in Pikachu onesies.

00:08:44.889 --> 00:08:47.519
The D-class were placed four meters apart.

00:08:47.519 --> 00:08:52.660
After a period of time, a tingling sensation
was reported in the arms and legs, akin to

00:08:52.660 --> 00:08:57.120
that pins-and-needles feeling you get when
your arms fall asleep, or when you get shocked

00:08:57.120 --> 00:08:58.800
by static electricity.

00:08:58.800 --> 00:09:03.620
The next one had four D-Class, all dressed
similar to the previous group.

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:09.050
Instead of being meters apart, they were asked
to hold hands, which the D-Class begrudgingly

00:09:09.050 --> 00:09:10.070
did.

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:14.220
Severe migraines were reported, as well as
“throbbing pain in the cranium and lower

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:15.959
jowls of the face”.

00:09:15.959 --> 00:09:20.259
Near the tailbone, some D-Class reported a
dull aching.

00:09:20.259 --> 00:09:26.000
Most curiously, several areas on their body
had begun to change in skin coloration.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:28.400
Namely, a mustard yellow.

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:32.850
Eventually, the Foundation began to test for
an affiliation or emotional connection to

00:09:32.850 --> 00:09:34.600
the Pokémon franchise.

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:39.200
Could that be the key to understanding SCP-5254?

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:42.949
Another four D-Class, all noted Pokémon fans,
were brought in.

00:09:42.949 --> 00:09:47.480
One had owned a copy of Pokémon Yellow for
the GameBoy when he was a child, and another

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:50.930
had a high-leveled account on the Pokémon
GO app.

00:09:50.930 --> 00:09:55.160
The Foundation discovered that these D-Class
reported muscle spasms along the extent of

00:09:55.160 --> 00:10:00.180
their spines, with one complaining of tightness
in their chest before coughing up tufts of

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:05.269
fur, and another physically recoiling upon
an attempt at physical contact, in fear they

00:10:05.269 --> 00:10:07.920
would electrically shock the researcher.

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:14.029
These experiments proved to be fruitful for
the Foundation, as they learned that SCP-5254

00:10:14.029 --> 00:10:15.690
was irreversible.

00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:20.800
Removing the clothing or items did not result
in the transformative properties of SCP-5254

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:22.000
reversing.

00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:27.279
Furthermore, the testing went on beyond this
point, just to cover all possible bases of

00:10:27.279 --> 00:10:32.399
what SCP-5254 was before the details were
properly ironed out.

00:10:32.399 --> 00:10:37.769
A total of 56 D-Class personnel were lost
during these experiments, and testing paused

00:10:37.769 --> 00:10:42.860
due to concern by Foundation higher-ups of
a potential security breach and damage being

00:10:42.860 --> 00:10:44.930
done to the site’s power grid.

00:10:44.930 --> 00:10:51.639
But most importantly, a connection to the
Pokémon brand was what enabled SCP-5254 to

00:10:51.639 --> 00:10:53.300
truly take effect.

00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:57.990
That’s what occurred at the Outbreak Festival,
where the bodies of costumed Pikachu fanatics

00:10:57.990 --> 00:11:01.970
fused into their costumes and barreled towards
the crowd.

00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:08.110
Now that the Foundation understood the “how”
of SCP-5254, they still had to get to the

00:11:08.110 --> 00:11:09.110
“why”.

00:11:09.110 --> 00:11:13.819
Even by Foundation standards, this is a pretty
odd and random anomaly.

00:11:13.819 --> 00:11:18.410
Did the answers lie with Gamefreak or The
Pokémon Company itself?

00:11:18.410 --> 00:11:23.230
After the Festival incident, the Foundation
put web-probes into the servers of The Pokémon

00:11:23.230 --> 00:11:27.870
Company’s Japanese branch, and had their
web crawlers scan through millions of correspondence

00:11:27.870 --> 00:11:30.949
emails to find any hint of unusual behavior.

00:11:30.949 --> 00:11:35.620
A series of emails between major shareholders
in the company were found.

00:11:35.620 --> 00:11:41.620
The first was from Kimishima Tatsumi, the
CEO of Nintendo, the overseeing company above

00:11:41.620 --> 00:11:45.890
the Pokémon company, and Tsunekazu Ishihara,
the latter’s CEO.

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:48.230
It read:
“Do not ask questions.

00:11:48.230 --> 00:11:52.509
If this "Ser Viper" wants manpower for his
project, give it to him.

00:11:52.509 --> 00:11:55.939
Our society will not miss these irrelevant
individuals.

00:11:55.939 --> 00:12:01.199
“He, whoever he claims to be, may be charging
us a small fortune, but at least he seems

00:12:01.199 --> 00:12:05.250
genuinely interested in bringing our creations
to life.”

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:07.600
Bringing their creations to life?

00:12:07.600 --> 00:12:08.980
How curious.

00:12:08.980 --> 00:12:13.980
The email was dated to 2017, two years before
the outbreak incident.

00:12:13.980 --> 00:12:16.750
The Foundation decided to dig deeper.

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:21.490
Another email from 2017, exchanged between
the two individuals months after the first:

00:12:21.490 --> 00:12:25.760
“Tuesday will mark the fifth visit by the
Fukushima Orphanage to our headquarters.

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:30.540
I told the press it's part of our global outreach
programme to spread the joy of Pokémon to

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:31.629
the rest of the world.

00:12:31.629 --> 00:12:33.769
Early results have been positive.

00:12:33.769 --> 00:12:37.580
I should have a specimen to show you the next
time we meet in Tokyo.

00:12:37.580 --> 00:12:40.120
Your daughter likes Eevee, yes?”

00:12:40.120 --> 00:12:44.540
It seemed like these executives were talking
about creating real Pokémon, somehow!

00:12:44.540 --> 00:12:47.389
What did the orphanage have to do with this?

00:12:47.389 --> 00:12:48.540
Another email read:

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:51.420
“Play anytime, anywhere, with anyone.

00:12:51.420 --> 00:12:55.610
Yes, the slogan for the Switch is very apt
for what we're trying to accomplish.

00:12:55.610 --> 00:12:57.120
Your marketing team deserves a raise.

00:12:57.120 --> 00:13:03.589
I am pleased to report Pokémon Go2 has hit
750 million unique downloads in July and 5

00:13:03.589 --> 00:13:06.420
million daily average users this past week.

00:13:06.420 --> 00:13:09.759
The popularity of the franchise continues
to grow.

00:13:09.759 --> 00:13:15.040
Think of the possibilities once we integrate
Augmented Reality (AR) technology into the

00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:20.139
project: Altaria as a clean and efficient
form of air transportation, Charizard serving

00:13:20.139 --> 00:13:25.899
in the Self-Defense Forces, and yes, Pikachu
making our reliance on nuclear energy a thing

00:13:25.899 --> 00:13:26.899
of the past.

00:13:26.899 --> 00:13:31.050
Soon, Pokémon will come to life before our
very eyes.”

00:13:31.050 --> 00:13:35.041
The Foundation couldn’t believe something
as absurd as creating real Pokémon was a

00:13:35.041 --> 00:13:37.970
genuine possibility for these companies.

00:13:37.970 --> 00:13:40.579
It was going on right beneath their noses.

00:13:40.579 --> 00:13:46.029
But the emails from 2018 began to show cracks
in the Pokémon Company and Nintendo’s plans.

00:13:46.029 --> 00:13:48.259
“The accidents are growing in number.

00:13:48.259 --> 00:13:51.070
Are you sure "Ser Viper" has everything under
control?

00:13:51.070 --> 00:13:53.509
We cannot hide these incidents from the public
forever.

00:13:53.509 --> 00:13:57.209
We already have our hands full trying to catch
the runaways.

00:13:57.209 --> 00:14:00.800
If we don't take action soon, more people
will get hurt.

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:04.819
Or worse: the Pokémon brand will be tarnished
forever.”

00:14:04.819 --> 00:14:09.660
Whoever was responsible for creating Pokémon
for the companies was going by the alias of

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:14.260
“Ser Viper”, and it seemed like their
experiments weren’t working the way they

00:14:14.260 --> 00:14:15.260
planned.

00:14:15.260 --> 00:14:19.439
An email directly addressed to Ser Viper fully
encapsulated the Pokémon Company’s disgust

00:14:19.439 --> 00:14:24.360
at the individual once they realized the experiments
weren’t succeeding in creating an immersive,

00:14:24.360 --> 00:14:27.290
fun Pokémon experience in the real world.

00:14:27.290 --> 00:14:32.529
“You promised us Pokémon as pets and companions
- not these mutations!

00:14:32.529 --> 00:14:37.699
I've had to recall thousands of faulty merchandise,
with tens of thousands of defective products

00:14:37.699 --> 00:14:39.660
still circulating the market.

00:14:39.660 --> 00:14:42.600
Just what kind of sorcery have you forced
upon our hands?

00:14:42.600 --> 00:14:47.380
The government is breathing down my neck,
Tatsumi-san has had to resign and I'm starting

00:14:47.380 --> 00:14:50.300
to hear about this "Foundation" poking around.

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:54.589
Tell me the truth - is there any way to reverse
the effects?

00:14:54.589 --> 00:14:57.140
Or have you doomed us all?

00:14:57.140 --> 00:15:01.029
“SerViper1995”, as their screen name read,
responded with this:

00:15:01.029 --> 00:15:03.509
“I don't know what to tell you.

00:15:03.509 --> 00:15:09.740
I've given the people what they want - only
true fans will get a Pokémon of their own.

00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:13.649
Your company was the very best at building
your brand.

00:15:13.649 --> 00:15:14.649
Congratulations.

00:15:14.649 --> 00:15:18.680
Today, Pokémon has taken over our hearts
and minds.

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:22.740
Perhaps one day, we will see them take over
the world.”

00:15:22.740 --> 00:15:26.460
And with that, the company had cut off all
communication with “Ser Viper”.

00:15:26.460 --> 00:15:30.670
But now, the Foundation had to get to the
bottom of what was happening in those boardrooms

00:15:30.670 --> 00:15:32.139
and offices.

00:15:32.139 --> 00:15:34.009
Making Pokémon in real life?

00:15:34.009 --> 00:15:38.759
It sounded crazy, and from the way the emails
were worded, they had apparently succeeded

00:15:38.759 --> 00:15:43.010
in making something, even if they considered
it a failure.

00:15:43.010 --> 00:15:48.850
Three months later, after all of the research
on SCP-5254 was conducted, the Overseer Council

00:15:48.850 --> 00:15:54.959
authorized a raid on the Pokémon Company
offices in Minato City, Tokyo, on June 16th,

00:15:54.959 --> 00:15:55.959
2019.

00:15:55.959 --> 00:15:59.230
From the way the emails were written, they
had reason to believe that civilians were

00:15:59.230 --> 00:16:03.509
potentially being held against their will
and used in these experiments.

00:16:03.509 --> 00:16:07.809
Failure to deal with them now could potentially
spell disaster if they got out, and the cause

00:16:07.809 --> 00:16:11.769
of SCP-5254 wasn’t immediately neutralized.

00:16:11.769 --> 00:16:16.199
Following the Japanese government’s authorization
of the raid, a Foundation Mobile Task Force

00:16:16.199 --> 00:16:21.699
detachment from Epsilon-11 “Nine Tailed
Fox” was stationed outside the offices.

00:16:21.699 --> 00:16:25.900
The task force broke into the building through
the fire exit, and promptly cleared out tourists

00:16:25.900 --> 00:16:28.110
and civilians from the area.

00:16:28.110 --> 00:16:32.579
During the raid, they encountered a large
creature that resembled a Charizard, an orange,

00:16:32.579 --> 00:16:36.430
fire-breathing dragon Pokémon, that stopped
them in their tracks in the hallway.

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:42.319
Wings, an elongated snout, the perfect color,
it looked exactly as if a Charizard had leapt

00:16:42.319 --> 00:16:45.069
from the screen and into real life.

00:16:45.069 --> 00:16:49.529
It spewed combustible, orange liquid at the
team, but they quickly dispatched it with

00:16:49.529 --> 00:16:52.999
ease, using their weapons to put some water
on the Pokémon’s fire.

00:16:52.999 --> 00:16:57.910
Well, the water was actually a salvo of bullets,
but the metaphor still works.

00:16:57.910 --> 00:17:02.249
Most of the building was cleared, and those
inside detained for further questioning.

00:17:02.249 --> 00:17:05.810
But then the team came to a set of steel doors.

00:17:05.810 --> 00:17:10.930
Inside was a room littered with toys, brightly
colored walls, and large, metal cages.

00:17:10.930 --> 00:17:13.450
But then the team came to a set of steel doors.

00:17:13.450 --> 00:17:17.010
Inside was a room littered with toys, brightly
colored walls, and large, metal cages.

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:20.910
Ser Viper’s failed experiments, clearly.

00:17:20.910 --> 00:17:25.070
Entities at various stages of SCP-5254 transformation.

00:17:25.070 --> 00:17:27.300
One resembled a Vulpix, a fox pokemon.

00:17:27.300 --> 00:17:31.770
It had engorged eye sockets and blood flowing
down their cheeks.

00:17:31.770 --> 00:17:36.760
Another cage had a boy with cheek-bones protruding
high and sideways, pulling thin skin over

00:17:36.760 --> 00:17:38.650
the rest of his face.

00:17:38.650 --> 00:17:43.610
Another had a large bear-like entity with
serrated claws, with alternate fingers peeling

00:17:43.610 --> 00:17:45.920
and decomposing underneath.

00:17:45.920 --> 00:17:50.270
Most horrifying of all were a pair inside
cages near the other side of the room.

00:17:50.270 --> 00:17:55.710
A girl with an extended, flattened, engorged
tongue, which pooled drool on the floor at

00:17:55.710 --> 00:17:56.710
her feet.

00:17:56.710 --> 00:18:01.800
She was made to resemble a Lickitung, a Pokemon
with a similarly large tongue.

00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:07.180
Another was an elongated purple snake, like
the Pokemon Arbok, except its head was that

00:18:07.180 --> 00:18:08.180
of a toddler.

00:18:08.180 --> 00:18:12.220
It writhed back and forth, bawling and screaming.

00:18:12.220 --> 00:18:16.540
The team requested immediate medical pick-up
to remove the specimens from the room.

00:18:16.540 --> 00:18:21.860
Wherever Ser Viper, the individual responsible
for this, was, the Foundation could not locate

00:18:21.860 --> 00:18:22.860
them.

00:18:22.860 --> 00:18:27.580
The Foundation contained the experiments,
and detained Mr. Ishihara, the CEO of the

00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:28.580
company.

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:30.720
He was brought back to the research site for
an interview.

00:18:30.720 --> 00:18:35.660
Ishihara claimed not to know of the experiment's
existence, but he quickly broke down.

00:18:35.660 --> 00:18:38.940
When asked about Ser Viper, Ishihara had this
to say.

00:18:38.940 --> 00:18:41.190
“We didn't ask too many questions.

00:18:41.190 --> 00:18:46.270
When we found out what he was doing to the
children, we terminated his contract immediately.

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:47.800
But the damage had been done.

00:18:47.800 --> 00:18:51.730
Later, we discovered he had already tampered
with our production lines and distribution

00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:52.730
infrastructure.

00:18:52.730 --> 00:18:57.030
At this point, it's impossible to tell which
products have been affected on the market.”

00:18:57.030 --> 00:19:02.300
Following this, global coordination between
Nintendo, the Foundation, and The Pokemon

00:19:02.300 --> 00:19:08.000
Company in an attempt to figure out a solution
to products that were affected by SCP-5254

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:09.990
is presently ongoing.

00:19:09.990 --> 00:19:15.940
All attempts to contact “SerViper1995”’s
email result in the same automated message:

00:19:15.940 --> 00:19:17.400
“Happy hunting.

00:19:17.400 --> 00:19:20.580
But even you can't catch 'em all.”

00:19:20.580 --> 00:19:26.890
Now go watch “SCP-3108 The Nerfing Gun”
and “SCP-387 - The Living Lego” for more

00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:31.540
Kid-friendly Franchises twisted into anomalous
entities contained by the SCP Foundation!

